rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Montana statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>70-25-202(1)(a): landlord must give the departing tenant a written list of rent due and damage/cleaning charges within 30 days after termination of tenancy or surrender, with payment of the remaining deposit. (MCA 70-25-202; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0250/part_0020/section_0020/0700-0250-0020-0020.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>70-25-202(1)(b): if after inspection there is no damage, no cleaning needed, no unpaid rent and no unpaid utilities, the deposit must be returned within 10 days. (MCA 70-25-202; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0250/part_0020/section_0020/0700-0250-0020-0020.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>70-25-203: a landlord who fails to give the written list forfeits all rights to withhold any deposit for damages or cleaning. (MCA 70-25-203; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0250/part_0020/section_0030/0700-0250-0020-0030.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>70-24-441(2): landlord or tenant may end a month-to-month tenancy with at least 30 days&#x27; written notice. (MCA 70-24-441; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0040/section_0410/0700-0240-0040-0410.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>70-24-312(3)(a): landlord must give at least 24 hours&#x27; notice to enter, except emergency or impracticable, and enter only at reasonable times. (MCA 70-24-312; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0030/section_0120/0700-0240-0030-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>70-24-431(1): landlord may not retaliate by raising rent, decreasing services, or bringing/threatening an action for possession after tenant complains to a housing-code agency, complains in writing of a 70-24-303 violation, or joins a tenant organization. (MCA 70-24-431; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0040/section_0310/0700-0240-0040-0310.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-probate-laws/'>Montana Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Montana guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0250/part_0020/section_0020/0700-0250-0020-0020.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 70-25-202</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0250/part_0020/section_0030/0700-0250-0020-0030.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 70-25-203</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0040/section_0410/0700-0240-0040-0410.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 70-24-441</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0030/section_0120/0700-0240-0030-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 70-24-312</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0240/part_0040/section_0310/0700-0240-0040-0310.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 70-24-431</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights", "rank_math_description": "Montana landlord tenant law and tenant rights: deposits, notices, entry and selling a rented house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana tenant rights"}, {"slug": "montana-probate-laws", "title": "Montana Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Probate Laws: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Probate Laws sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Probate Laws offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Montana probate law decides who inherits when there is no will, when a small estate can skip full probate, and who can sign a deed for an inherited house.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>72-2-112: surviving spouse takes the entire intestate estate if no descendant or parent survives, or if all decedent&#x27;s descendants are also the spouse&#x27;s; first $300,000 plus 3/4 of balance if only a parent survives; first $150,000 plus 1/2 of balance if some decedent&#x27;s descendants are not the spouse&#x27;s. (MCA 72-2-112; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0020/part_0010/section_0120/0720-0020-0010-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>72-3-1101: small estate affidavit for personal property - probate estate (less liens) not over $100,000, 30 days since death, no personal representative application pending. (MCA 72-3-1101; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0030/part_0110/section_0010/0720-0030-0110-0010.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>72-3-613(6),(23): unless restricted by the will or a formal-proceeding order, a personal representative may sell, mortgage or lease real or personal estate property, including land, at public or private sale. (MCA 72-3-613; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0030/part_0060/section_0130/0720-0030-0060-0130.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Montana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Montana guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0020/part_0010/section_0120/0720-0020-0010-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 72-2-112</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0030/part_0110/section_0010/0720-0030-0110-0010.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 72-3-1101</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0720/chapter_0030/part_0060/section_0130/0720-0030-0060-0130.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCA 72-3-613</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Probate Laws, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-probate-laws/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales", "rank_math_description": "Montana probate laws: who inherits without a will, small estate rules, deadlines and selling an inherited house. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana probate laws"}]